# KOB production deploy lock

trykob.com (`kobkob`, site id `6348ca5b-9101-4ad6-bb07-f4ec29dda60c`) must **never** be published with `netlify deploy --prod`, drag-and-drop, or API deploys from this or any other repo (BELLY, plotapi, Joinwoods, etc.).

Allowed: git push to `aibcdev/kobOS` `main` (Netlify Git integration).

Forbidden:
- `npx netlify-cli deploy --prod`
- `netlify deploy --prod`
- `npm run netlify:deploy` with `--prod`
- Restoring or publishing a deploy whose title is not KOB

If production is wrong, restore a **KOB Next.js** deploy or wait for a Git build. Do not "fix" it by CLI-uploading another project.

Netlify site settings to keep: **Enforce Git-based production deploys**, publish directory **`.next`**, empty `package_path`, Next plugin only in `netlify.toml`.
